[statement]
Reduced from a layered request over Alpine v3.24 (`main` and `community`,
2026-11-08): `llvm-test-utils`'s closure from v3.23 installed and asked at
a later version. The later `llvm-test-utils` needs `python3~3.14`, which
the repository offers. Installed are `python3` 3.12, `python3-pyc`, whose
`install_if` names `python3` at that version exactly and which needs
`pyc`, and `pyc`; no repository offers either at another version. apk
refuses, keeping `python3` at 3.12, where it could upgrade `python3` and
remove the package whose condition no longer holds. Observed; the rule is
not yet known.

[repository]
P:llvm-test-utils
V:22-r0
D:llvm22-test-utils

P:llvm22-test-utils
V:22.1.3-r1
D:python3 python3~3.14

P:llvm22-test-utils-pyc
V:22.1.3-r1
i:llvm22-test-utils=22.1.3-r1 pyc

P:python3
V:3.14.10-r1

[installed]
P:python3
V:3.12.16-r0

P:pyc
V:3.12.16-r0

P:python3-pyc
V:3.12.16-r0
D:pyc
i:python3=3.12.16-r0

P:llvm21-test-utils
V:21.1.2-r1
D:python3~3.12

P:llvm-test-utils
V:21-r0
D:llvm21-test-utils

[request]
llvm-test-utils>21-r0

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   python3-3.12.16-r0:
|     breaks: llvm22-test-utils-22.1.3-r1[python3~3.14]
|     satisfies: llvm22-test-utils-22.1.3-r1[python3]
refused
